{
  "documentation": [
    "The shared-name contract (docs/FRONTEND.md, Shared names). A name that more",
    "than one surface spells is declared here once, and tests/test_shared_names.py",
    "derives the same map from the tree and holds the two to equality. A rename",
    "that reaches three surfaces and misses the fourth changes the derived map and",
    "fails make check.",
    "",
    "Each value is the exact set of surface kinds that spell the name, in the",
    "order: template (Jinja), stylesheet (page CSS), client (.mjs modules),",
    "python (src/election_guide, including rendering/browser.py's CDP audit",
    "probes), test (the Python and Node tests; the rendered fixtures under",
    "tests/js/fixtures are excluded as generated output).",
    "",
    "This file is not a ratchet. tests/frontend_ratchets.json records",
    "grandfathered debt that only shrinks and that the epic's closeout deletes;",
    "the shared-name contract is permanent and moves in both directions, so it",
    "lives beside that file rather than inside it.",
    "",
    "data_attributes: every data-* name on more than one surface.",
    "",
    "class_names: every authored class name that reaches executable code -- a",
    "client module or a Python probe string. A class only a template and a",
    "stylesheet share is out of scope: that pair is every class in the codebase,",
    "and a miss there renders unstyled rather than passing quietly.",
    "",
    "breakpoints: every @media width threshold that executable code restates.",
    "Outside a stylesheet a bare integer counts only where the same line names a",
    "width, which is how rendering/browser.py restates one.",
    "",
    "The scan is textual, so a name a comment mentions counts as spelled there.",
    "That keeps prose about a name accurate when it is renamed and never lets a",
    "real use hide behind one; no entry below is present only for that reason.",
    "Surfaces are recorded by kind rather than by file, so a rename that misses a",
    "second file of the same kind is left to that language's own checker --- tsc",
    "and the module tests for the client, pyright for Python. The boundary",
    "between languages is the one nothing else can see, and is what this holds.",
    "",
    "Grade strings are deliberately absent. They have a Python origin",
    "(scoring/models.py's Grade) and reach the client through the payload",
    "generator issue #236 landed; a second declaration here would give one",
    "vocabulary two generators."
  ],
